- review/prompts/ adapts review-rubric prose from TauCetiProject/TauCetiReview
  (https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCetiReview) at commit
  b9539a39556d34b3e3bf6199d0da7b4e7d5d4c27 (2026-07-22), licensed Apache-2.0.
  The passages are independently reworded (not copied verbatim) and re-mapped to
  this repo's finding categories and severity/verdict tiers:
    * _operating_contract.md "Assume a same-model author" ← rubrics/_common.md
      ("Assume an adversarial author");
    * lean4_checklist.md items 10–13 (vacuity/placeholders, extensionality/free
      data, reuse-search, robust automation) ← rubrics/correctness.md,
      api-design.md, reuse.md, proof-quality.md respectively.
  Per-item provenance is recorded inline in those files.

- review/ two-stage CI security scripts and workflow templates (Session 18) are
  adapted from TauCetiProject/TauCeti
  (https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti) at commit
  92c79e5e0a618f8c5c2b9909be1ce50f6891dde7 (2026-07-23), licensed Apache-2.0. That
  repo declares no copyright holder and ships no NOTICE (so there is no Apache §4(d)
  content to propagate); the adapted files carry an in-file `Adapted from …@92c79e5`
  header and a §4(b) change note. Files:
    * review/scope_guard.sh ← .github/workflows/pr-build.yml (the "Scope guard" step),
      extracted as a standalone script and hardened (any-depth allowlist, >3000-file
      cap, explicit gh-error/SIGPIPE fail-close).
    * review/authorize.sh ← .github/workflows/review.yml (the authorize step),
      extracted as a standalone script and hardened (distinct exit codes for
      API-error vs deny, 404-non-collaborator handling, env-not-inline injection safety).
    * review/pr-build.yml ← .github/workflows/pr-build.yml (generalised two-stage
      build template: pull_request_target overlay + scope guard + landrun + status handoff).
    * review/review.yml ← .github/workflows/review.yml (generalised privileged-review
      template: workflow_run/issue_comment, authorize, secrets only after build-status pass).
    * review/scripts/sandbox-build.sh ← scripts/sandbox-build.sh (generalised confined
      build; project-specific audits left to the adopting repo).
    * review/scripts/sandbox-selftest.sh ← the inline landrun self-test in pr-build.yml
      (extracted + hardened: positive control, no unsatisfiable UDP-deny, fail-closed host).
  landrun (github.com/Zouuup/landrun, MIT) is used as a pinned + SHA256-verified binary,
  not vendored.

